{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStep","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStepO","text":"MXLStep","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"text","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","text":"MXLPosition","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = MXLPosition(), ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = MXLFont(), ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil)","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"value"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Indicates how the bass should appear in a score if not using the element contents.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"text"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The font-style can be normal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text font vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"font"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"color"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLBass.Step","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct\/init(value:text:position:font:color:)"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStepO","text":"MXLStep","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"text","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","text":"MXLPosition","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBassV4StepV5value4text8position4font5colorAeA7MXLStepO_SSSgAA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgtcfc","symbolKind":"init","role":"symbol","title":"init(value:text:position:font:color:)"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct\/init(value:text:position:font:color:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bass type is used to indicate a bass note in popular music chord symbols, e.g. G\/C. It is generally not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in functional harmony, as inversion is generally not used in pop chord symbols. As with root, it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"divided into step and alter elements, similar to pitches. The arrangement attribute specifies where the bass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is displayed relative to what precedes it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBass"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLBass","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBass"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStep":{"title":"MXLStep","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStep","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstep","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStep","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStep","abstract":[{"text":"The step type represents a step of the diatonic scale, represented using the English letters A through G.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass/Step-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bass-step type represents the pitch step of the bass of the current chord within the harmony element. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text attribute indicates how the bass should appear in a score if not using the element contents."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Step"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLBass.Step","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Step"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swi